<title>UK: Rolls-Royce wins $110 mln order from Monarch.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce wins $110 mln order from Monarch.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and aerospace group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Thursday it had won a $110 million order for Trent and V2500 jet engines from Britain's Monarch Airlines.</p>
<p>Monarch has ordered two A330-200 aircraft for delivery in March or April 1999 which will be powered by the Trent engines, Rolls-Royce said. Monarch is also buying two A321-200s to be powered by the V2500 engines.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
